+every evaluated model (e.g. `runs/20260701_170411` doc_causal simplewiki:
+`mean_nll=403.9`, `perplexity=2.56e175`). A per-token mean NLL is bounded by
+`ln(vocab)=ln(50257)≈10.8`, so ~404 is ~40× over the theoretical max — the
+aggregate is summing where it should be averaging, or the per-doc `mean_nll`
+from `eval/scoring.py:score_doc` is malformed for these checkpoints. Chase it
+down:
